This is dynamic programming done right. It involves a few steps.

First, calculate the cost of each individual number by iterating over the numbers once. Next, for each pair of numbers, calculate the cost of adding them together and store the result.

Finally, look at every possible pair of numbers and determine which combination has the lowest cost by summing the costs of the individual numbers plus the lowest pair found so far. This way, the algorithm ensures that it is always looking for the most efficient pair at each step.
